{"id": "EUVD-2026-102566", "enisaUuid": "6011efd5-f08c-3063-97db-0277f91d230b", "description": "Nezha from 2.1.0 before 2.3.15 contains a host header injection vulnerability in mintTransferTool that builds fs.download_url and fs.upload_url transfer URLs from the unvalidated Host header. Attackers who control the Host header seen on a victim's MCP request can redirect file uploads or capture one-time download tokens and replay them to exfiltrate files.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T01:17:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T02:07:31", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/nezhahq/nezha/security/advisories/GHSA-rj3w-jrj7-x7c3", "https://github.com/nezhahq/nezha/commit/36b742a7e9a81ed782363dd19efd77b7030fbd0f", "https://github.com/nezhahq/nezha/commit/c726930833937a0aebb2a924064f236faea889f6", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nezha-2.1.0-before-2.3.15-host-header-injection-via-mcp-transfer-tools"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111385", "GHSA-7fqg-h9rw-ww63"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7f1a80dc-68de-33c3-829e-c5485c52a04e", "product": {"name": "nezha", "vendor": {"name": "nezhahq"}}, "product_version": "2.1.0 <2.3.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d43ea5e0-a004-30af-9f98-88aa7d464057", "vendor": {"name": "nezhahq"}}], "isExploited": false}